<title>FRANCE: French mobile phone use up to 2.2 mln in November.</title>
<headline>French mobile phone use up to 2.2 mln in November.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The total number of mobile phones in France increased by 5.6 percent to 2,238,400 in November while the number of people using digital mobile phones rose by 6.6 percent to more than two million at 2,019,000.</p>
<p>The Ministry of Post and Telecommunications said in a statement that France Telecom's Itineris digital service had a five percent increase in the month to 1,211,900 while Generale des Eaux SFR rose 8.3 percent to 715,400. Bouygues Telecom had 72,100 subscribers, up 18.8 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
